WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.800
- Hello, hello, hello.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.940
We're over a month into this quarantine

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:05.340
and it's a pretty stressful time,

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.780
like it's stressful for everybody,

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.290
not just us healthcare workers.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.280
There's all sorts of new
challenges that we're facing

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.700
that we simply didn't expect,
so I wanted to make a video

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.486
where I can help you get
through this difficult time

00:00:14.486 --> 00:00:16.440
as the best version of yourself.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.020
I wanna give a huge thank you to Nike

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.110
for sponsoring this video,

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.300
where I'm gonna be giving
you some strategies

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.563
to optimize both your
physical and mental health.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.460
In order for me to give
you comprehensive advice

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.040
on self care, we have to talk
about both the mind and body,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.380
in fact, I don't like that
they're separate words,

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.580
it should be mind-body

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.130
'cause there's so intimately connected.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.578
Any change you make to your mental health

00:00:40.578 --> 00:00:42.230
will show physical effects,

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.710
any change you make to
your physical health,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.870
will show mental effects.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.090
First, let's focus up here.

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:49.370
The mindset that I want you
to have during quarantine,

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:52.790
when we're generally not moving
around much is on movement.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.660
I want you motivated and
excited to go for that run,

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.949
to do that exercise regimen.

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:59.150
Let's get you started with these few tips.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.110
Make tech your friend, there's
all sorts of meditation

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:04.670
and mindfulness apps that
can help you get motivated.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.150
What I like to do is
listen to the Nike Run Club

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.340
Audio Guided Runs, they have athletes

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.620
and motivational speakers
like Coach Bennett,

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:14.950
to really boost my mood and my
performance at the same time.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.950
Stay on routine.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.710
For many of us, jobs
give our day structure

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.368
and with so many people being out of work

00:01:21.368 --> 00:01:23.430
or their work being disrupted,

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.760
it's very easy to go to sleep at any time,

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.027
wake up at any time of the day,

00:01:27.027 --> 00:01:30.430
but that actually adds a
layer of chaos to your life

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.650
that your mind and body both don't like.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.570
So create a routine and stick to it,

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.160
plus, you'll make your life easier.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:38.550
Oh, it's five o'clock, gotta exercise

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:39.720
'cause that's just what I do.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.440
Understand willpower.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.310
Too many people assume
they have to be motivated

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.760
in order to get an action,
action proceeds willpower,

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.550
you need to take that first step,

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:51.390
do the first exercise class

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:54.400
in order for you to get some
willpower for the next time,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.820
doesn't have to be anything huge,

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.290
just something small that you
can check off as a success

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.191
in order to refill the willpower tank.

00:02:00.191 --> 00:02:02.800
Stay social, physical distancing

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.700
does not mean social isolation.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.140
Humans are social beings, we
crave that type of connection,

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:10.410
FaceTime a friend, go on a Skype meeting

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.950
with all of your family
members to talk some drama,

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.910
go on a real date, take it seriously,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.030
don't just get on a couch in pajamas,

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.596
get a meal, get all dressed up.

00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:21.300
Celebrate human resilience.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.130
Humans are great at
bouncing back from adversity

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:27.110
and a pandemic like this is
the definition of adversity.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.250
In fact, what we've seen
with scientific research

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.490
is evidence for post traumatic growth.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.700
So while most humans,

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.060
when they go through something traumatic,

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:37.940
their baseline drops and then
they can bounce back to normal

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.890
once the adversity ends but
in post traumatic growth,

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.370
you actually see this baseline drop off,

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.000
and then come up even higher.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.970
So we can come out of this
pandemic as better humans,

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:49.220
those who appreciate

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:51.920
the things we once took
for granted, let's do that.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.943
Get physical.
(grunting)

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.320
Folks, you gotta keep your body in motion,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.550
you gotta stay moving.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:03.930
I know it's hard now during quarantine,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.560
when gyms are closed and
perhaps running outside

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.590
isn't so safe, you still have to do it,

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:10.920
otherwise you're gonna
develop aches, pains,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.100
your moods gonna suffer.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.640
Let's start with something
I've fallen in love with,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.230
online exercise classes courtesy
of the Nike Training Club.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.839
- [Instructor] Your head, hips and ankles

00:03:19.839 --> 00:03:22.390
should all be in a nice straight line,

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.110
sit back into your hips
and lower yourself down

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.890
so your upper legs are
parallel to the ground.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.110
Stay relaxed in Child's Pose.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.660
- You have to make due with what you have

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:34.580
and I have a stationary
bike, this is perfect

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.270
for getting a high intensity
interval workout it.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.680
For those of you who don't know,

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.750
an HIIT workout is when
we alternate long periods

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:42.963
of low intensity exercise,

00:03:42.963 --> 00:03:45.360
followed by short bursts
of high intensity.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.688
Low intensity is slow, low effort,

00:03:47.688 --> 00:03:49.830
high intensity is like all outbursts

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:50.900
for a short period of time

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.030
and trust me in like 20, 30 minutes,

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:55.720
you can get a solid workout
in, where you're burning fat,

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:59.422
maintaining muscle, cardio,
strength training all in one

00:03:59.422 --> 00:04:01.460
and you don't need a
stationary bike for that.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:02.610
You could go on a treadmill,

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:04.460
you could even do it in your hallway.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.353
(lively music)

00:04:13.874 --> 00:04:16.707
(whistle blowing)

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:20.941
Everything I'm explaining to
you is about being adaptable,

00:04:20.941 --> 00:04:23.940
leaning into uncertainty and
making use of what you have.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.157
I know there's gonna be people
out there that are saying,

00:04:26.157 --> 00:04:28.487
"Look Mike, I appreciate
doing squats at home

00:04:28.487 --> 00:04:29.530
"but I need weights."

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.973
You make use with what
you have, what do I have?

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.953
- [Dog] Nice.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.110
- Okay, I'm obviously
joking, don't use your dog.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.600
You could use other things
this way, like sandbags.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:44.660
I have a sandbag to hold down the sea sand

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.790
and I have dog hair on me.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.040
Kettlebell swings, this
is actually pretty heavy

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:48.873
and it's a good workout.

00:04:48.873 --> 00:04:50.640
Okay, I get it, not
everyone has a sandbag,

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.290
almost everyone has a book bag

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.510
that you can load up with
heavy stuff, kettlebell swings.

00:04:55.510 --> 00:04:56.343
You see what I'm saying?

00:04:56.343 --> 00:04:57.910
Not everyone needs fancy gym equipment

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.950
in order to get a good workout.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:00.890
I'm out of breath already.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:02.133
Even though this is a quarantine,

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.423
we're in a pandemic, you
still can have a good time

00:05:04.423 --> 00:05:06.770
and stay fit, at the end of the day,

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.400
I'm a doctor and doctors
write a lot of prescriptions,

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.500
but prescriptions and
all medical treatments

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:14.750
